# Aston Martin V8 Vantage coupe, 2005-2017.
#
# The compact VH-platform Vantage: the wide low body, the long bonnet, the
# mesh grille, the pronounced rear diffuser and the twin exhausts. The coupe
# is modelled; the Roadster is a different body. The car photographed is the
# pre-facelift 4.3-litre car.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_Vantage_(2005)
#
# Dimensions 4.382 x 1.867 x 1.255 m, wheelbase 2.601 m.
#
# Shape reference: a dark blue UK V8 Vantage coupe in true side elevation and
# front three-quarter, and a black London car in rear three-quarter. The side
# and front are the same car; the rear is a different car of the same model.
#
# Colours: grade (c) for the N400 limited edition of 2007 (Lightning Silver
# and Karussell Orange); dark blue and black are the two photographed cars and
# are plain names. Grade (d) for the standard range, for which no UK colour
# chart was found. Weights 3, 3, 2, 2, total 10, provisional.
#
# Speed 280 km/h. Comfort 78/447, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 78. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2005 intro, retires staggered 2032-2035.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-vantage-2005.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-vantage-2005.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-vantage-2005/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the hatch lip is understated and the rear lamp and
# diffuser shapes need refinement. At 128 px the short overhangs, wide grille
# and glass hatch read as a V8 Vantage.


